{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 51, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass on the very day, HaShem brought out</b> — Since it said above (Exodus 12:42), \"It was a night of watching for HaShem, to bring them out of the land of Egypt,\" He came back and explained that they did not all leave the land at night, but rather that He granted them permission to depart and they were free men; but <b>on the very day</b> they went forth from all the territory of Egypt with all their hosts — the host of the women and the mixed multitude that joined them. And R. Abraham ibn Ezra explained that <b>\"And it came to pass on the very day, HaShem brought out</b> <b>the children of Israel from the land of Egypt\"</b> — this is what the text refers to when it says HaShem spoke to Moses, \"Sanctify to Me.\""], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:06:56.985908493Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}